{"id": "swebq0157", "pool": "swebq", "arm": "aggressive", "tier": "aggressive", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 3679539445, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "8c3af78f4533df26d66383d6216ec5cacb9faa8bb324f3d6a6d51641beeea3a9", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.5533501505851746, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 0, "query": "where did flemish people come from?", "input_path": "/data/bench_audio/swebq0157.wav", "input_sha256": "0df62984cf0229de611e96e99de366118d5ad8f6503d6a410593afcb3b546898", "input_samples": 28960, "input_s": 1.81, "n_real_chunks": 2, "score": 0.6352, "act": 0.9981, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "Flemish people come from Flanders, the Dutch-speaking northern region of present-day Belgium, with historical roots in the medieval County of Flanders. Ethnically and linguistically, they developed from a mix of early medieval populations in the Low Countries, especially Germanic-speaking groups such as the Franks, along with earlier local Gallo-Roman/Celtic populations. Their language, Flemish, is a group of Dutch dialects.", "expert_answer": "**Flemish people come from Flanders**, the Dutch-speaking northern region of present-day **Belgium**, with historical roots in the medieval **County of Flanders**.\n\nEthnically and linguistically, they developed from a mix of early medieval populations in the Low Countries, especially **Germanic-speaking groups such as the Franks**, along with earlier local **Gallo-Roman/Celtic** populations. Their language, **Flemish**, is a group of Dutch dialects.", "transcript": "Where did Flemish people come from?\n", "asr_s": 0.63, "expert_s": 3.3, "expert_input_samples": 28960, "expert_input_s": 1.81, "expert_input_sha256": "0df62984cf0229de611e96e99de366118d5ad8f6503d6a410593afcb3b546898", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 3.149, "relay_synth_ms": 11093,